    {
      "id": "badge-step-1",
      "tag": "shape",
      "position": [156, 572],
      "size": [28, 28],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "shape": { "kind": "ellipse" },
      "color": { "fill": "#e0e7ff" },
      "text": { "content": "1", "fontSize": 14, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "center", "color": "#4f46e5" },
      "verticalAlign": "center"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1-title",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [156, 612],
      "size": [208, 22],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": { "content": "Heat & Pressure", "fontSize": 15, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "left", "color": "#0f172a" },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1-body",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [156, 640],
      "size": [208, 110],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": {
        "content": "Fuel is heated to ~150 million °C.\nElectrons strip away, leaving a\nplasma of bare atomic nuclei.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fontWeight": "400",
        "align": "left",
        "color": "#64748b"
      },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "badge-step-2",
      "tag": "shape",
      "position": [428, 572],
      "size": [28, 28],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "shape": { "kind": "ellipse" },
      "color": { "fill": "#e0e7ff" },
      "text": { "content": "2", "fontSize": 14, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "center", "color": "#4f46e5" },
      "verticalAlign": "center"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2-title",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [428, 612],
      "size": [208, 22],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": { "content": "Coulomb Barrier", "fontSize": 15, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "left", "color": "#0f172a" },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2-body",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [428, 640],
      "size": [208, 110],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": {
        "content": "Both nuclei are positively charged,\nso they repel. They need enormous\nspeed — or quantum tunnelling.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fontWeight": "400",
        "align": "left",
        "color": "#64748b"
      },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "badge-step-3",
      "tag": "shape",
      "position": [700, 572],
      "size": [28, 28],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "shape": { "kind": "ellipse" },
      "color": { "fill": "#e0e7ff" },
      "text": { "content": "3", "fontSize": 14, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "center", "color": "#4f46e5" },
      "verticalAlign": "center"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3-title",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [700, 612],
      "size": [208, 22],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": { "content": "Strong Force Binds", "fontSize": 15, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "left", "color": "#0f172a" },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-3-body",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [700, 640],
      "size": [208, 110],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": {
        "content": "Within ~1 femtometre the strong\nnuclear force overcomes repulsion\nand fuses the nucleons together.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fontWeight": "400",
        "align": "left",
        "color": "#64748b"
      },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "badge-step-4",
      "tag": "shape",
      "position": [972, 572],
      "size": [28, 28],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "shape": { "kind": "ellipse" },
      "color": { "fill": "#e0e7ff" },
      "text": { "content": "4", "fontSize": 14, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "center", "color": "#4f46e5" },
      "verticalAlign": "center"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4-title",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [972, 612],
      "size": [208, 22],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": { "content": "Mass Becomes Energy", "fontSize": 15, "fontWeight": "600", "align": "left", "color": "#0f172a" },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "step-4-body",
      "tag": "text",
      "position": [972, 640],
      "size": [208, 110],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "a9",
      "text": {
        "content": "The new helium nucleus is slightly\nlighter than its parts. That mass\ndeficit emerges as kinetic energy.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "fontWeight": "400",
        "align": "left",
        "color": "#64748b"
      },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-where-fusion-happens",
      "tag": "sticky-note",
      "position": [136, 800],
      "size": [520, 96],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "b0",
      "color": { "fill": "#fef08a" },
      "text": {
        "content": "Where fusion happens\n• Sun's core: ~600 million tonnes of hydrogen fused every second.\n• On Earth: ITER (magnetic) and NIF (inertial) confinement.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "color": "#713f12"
      },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "note-net-gain",
      "tag": "sticky-note",
      "position": [680, 800],
      "size": [504, 96],
      "rotateZ": 0,
      "rank": "b0",
      "color": { "fill": "#bae6fd" },
      "text": {
        "content": "Net energy gain\nQ = energy out / energy in. Q > 1 is scientific breakeven — NIF reached it in December 2022.",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "color": "#075985"
      },
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    }
  ]
}